          "id": "12380165",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=keith.wong%40objectvalley.com",
            "name": "keith.wong@objectvalley.com",
            "key": "keith.wong@objectvalley.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Keith Wong",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Hong_Kong"
          },
          "body": "I received the following expiry date in SetCookie which DateParser v1.3 (from \nrc1) cannot handle:\n\nexpires=Mon, 18-08-2013 16:19:55 GMT\n\nIt uses numeric month value instead of the abbreviated form.  It is, I'm not \nsure if it is related, from a Microsoft-IIS/5.0 server.  Is it possible to \nadd \"EEE, dd-MM-yyyy HH:mm:ss z\" to DATE_PATTERNS?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=keith.wong%40objectvalley.com",
            "name": "keith.wong@objectvalley.com",
            "key": "keith.wong@objectvalley.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Keith Wong",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Asia/Hong_Kong"
          },
          "created": "2003-08-19T10:46:22.000+0000",
          "updated": "2003-08-19T10:46:22.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333749/comment/12380166",
          "id": "12380166",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Ortwin Glueck",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Zurich"
          },
          "body": "Well, it depends. Is this cookie date set by a faulty web application? Then you\nshould rather fix that application to use the standard date format. If however\nthis is coming from the server *directly* we will need to support it of course.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=oglueck",
            "name": "oglueck",
            "key": "oglueck",
            "avatarUrls": {
